SUMMARY:All the Lonely People by Mike Gayle
DESCRIPTION:Petaluma Book (And Brew) Club\nHubert Bird is not alone in bei
 ng alone.\n\nHe just needs to realize it.\n\nIn weekly phone calls to his 
 daughter in Australia\, widower Hubert Bird paints a picture of the perfec
 t retirement\, packed with fun\, friendship and fulfillment.\n\nBut Hubert
  Bird is lying.\n\nThe truth is day after day drags by without him seeing 
 a single soul.\n\nUntil\, that is\, he receives some good news - good news
  that in one way turns out to be the worst news ever\, news that will forc
 e him out again\, into a world he has long since turned his back on.\n\nNo
 w Hubert faces a seemingly impossible task: to make his real life resemble
  his fake life before the truth comes out.\nAlong the way Hubert stumbles 
 across a second chance at love\, renews a cherished friendship and finds h
 imself roped into an audacious community scheme that seeks to end loneline
 ss once and for all . . .
